# Day 4 – Learning Notes

## Lightning Web Components

Lightning Web Components (LWC) is Salesforce's modern framework for building user interfaces using web standards such as HTML, JavaScript and CSS.

## LWC Structure

An LWC normally contains three important files:

- HTML – Responsible for the page layout and UI.
- JavaScript – Responsible for variables, logic and events.
- Meta XML – Controls where the component can be used and exposed.

## Data Binding

Data binding connects JavaScript properties with the HTML template.

Example:

{studentName}

The value comes from the JavaScript property:

studentName = 'Rahul';

## Event Handling

I used a button click event to call a JavaScript method.

Example:

onclick={showWelcomeMessage}

The method changes the welcome message displayed on the page.

## Application Status

I used JavaScript to change:

Not Applied → Applied

No Apex or database was required for this activity.

## LWC and Apex

LWC is responsible for the user interface, while Apex can be used for server-side business logic and database operations.

## Main Learning

I learned how a Salesforce user interface can be created using LWC and how HTML, JavaScript and metadata work together to create a Lightning component.
